 4. 🔮 Scoop: Kennedy Center&#x27;s future 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Kennedy Center, seen from the Washington Monument on Monday. Photo: Andrew Harnik/Getty Images Earlier this month, Kennedy Center budget planners sketched out three options for its two-year renovation, including ways to keep the National Symphony Orchestra performing during construction, Axios D.C.'s Cuneyt Dil has learned. 

 Why it matters: The early plans — ahead of a board meeting tomorrow — offer a glimpse at how President Trump's allies are contemplating undertaking a controversial two-year closure. One scenario envisions the renowned 96-year-old orchestra — a fixture at the Kennedy Center — performing at "offsite alternate venues," according to a slide deck of budget plans obtained by Axios.

 Another scenario is more logistically complex. It'd keep the NSO performing inside the Kennedy Center — with a "phased" construction approach that could stretch beyond two years. A third, slimmed-down option appears to pause NSO programs. 👂 What we're hearing: Financial projections for the two-year renovation reveal keeping the NSO running costs $25 million annually.

 The forecasts are separate from the $250 million Trump anticipates spending on the renovation. Keep reading ... Get Axios Local , newsletters in 41 cities. 

 
 
