 7. 🏗️ Banks unleash infrastructure bucks 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 America's biggest financial firms are lining up to unlock vast sums of private capital for infrastructure investment, Axios' Neil Irwin writes. 

 Why it matters: Amid an AI buildout that is creating new strains on computing power, energy supplies and manufacturing capacity, major banks see opportunity for large-scale investment that could help satisfy those needs — and reward investors. A new $250 billion effort from Bank of America is the latest in a week packed with jaw-dropping funding announcements.

 Earlier this week, Morgan Stanley announced its own infrastructure initiative , which it said will total $1.5 trillion over a decade. Both firms tied their plans to honoring the 250th anniversary of the U.S. being celebrated this summer. Also this week: A remarkable announcement by chipmaker Nvidia of plans to finance $500 billion in AI infrastructure buildout in partnership with Apollo, BlackRock, Goldman Sachs and other Wall Street firms. Share this story . 

 
 
